steps.body:
For a < b:
- Open (a, b) = {x : a < x < b}
- Closed [a, b] = {x : a ≤ x ≤ b}
- Half-open [a, b) = {x : a ≤ x < b}, (a, b] = {x : a < x ≤ b}

The **length** of each is b − a. Infinity is never included: [2, ∞).

A **random experiment** has more than one possible outcome and the outcome cannot be predicted in advance. Each outcome is a **sample point**; the set of all outcomes is the **sample space S**.

- One coin: S = {H, T}
- Two coins: {HH, HT, TH, TT}
- One die: {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}; two dice: 36 ordered pairs.
